# Shortlinks. These are read off a screen - livestream lower thirds, slides,
# email - so they have to stay short and stay ours to repoint.
#
# 302, not 301: a permanent redirect gets cached by browsers and intermediaries,
# and the whole point of owning the shortlink is being able to change where it
# goes without chasing down every place it was already printed.
/discord https://discord.gg/puArEQHYN9 302
/discord/ https://discord.gg/puArEQHYN9 302

# /ph used to be a Pages Function because its destination depended on the
# go-live clock: before launch only the discussion page had a Follow button.
# That clock is long past and the awards are permanent, so the destination is
# now one stable URL and this belongs here as a static rule, not a runtime
# server. No query string on the destination, so a caller can still tag its own
# placement the way the Function allowed - /ph?utm_content=stream is forwarded.
/ph https://www.producthunt.com/products/construct-computer 302
/ph/ https://www.producthunt.com/products/construct-computer 302

